{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"zotero":1,"inscriptions":7,"isBulletin":294},{"title":2,"author":3,"date":4,"citation":5,"uri":6},"Iscrizione agonale di Heloros","Calderone","1949","\u003Cspan>S. Calderone, «Iscrizione agonale di Heloros», \u003Ci>Epigraphica\u003C/i> 10 (1949): 146–49\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/TIXRNSM3",[8],{"file":9,"uri":9,"title":10,"status":11,"editions":13,"editionAuthor":25,"type":26,"objectType":30,"material":34,"condition":42,"layoutDesc":44,"handNote":53,"date":200,"places":205,"geo":215,"country":210,"provenance":207,"provenanceGeo":219,"region":222,"settlement":223,"repository":224,"idno":228,"textLang":231,"tmNumber":15,"facsimile":235,"letterHeights":242,"publications":258,"zotero":266,"keywords":274,"html":286,"bibl":287,"bulletinDateSort":292,"citedRangeSort":293,"languageSort":232,"materialSort":35,"typeSort":27},"ISic001476","Inscription recording the neaniskoi of the gymnasium",{"_":12},"draft",[14,17,19,21,23],{"_":15,"type":16},"644986","TM",{"type":18},"EDR",{"type":20},"EDH",{"type":22},"EDCS",{"type":24},"PHI",null,{"_":27,"ana":28,"ref":29},"List","#function.list","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Names",{"_":31,"ana":32,"ref":33},"stele.","#object.stele","https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/250",{"_":35,"ana":36,"type":37,"subtype":38,"resp":40,"ref":41},"limestone","#material.inorganic.stone.sedimentary_rock.limestone.calcarenite.whitish","stone.limestone.non-polishable.whitish",[39],"unspecified","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html",{"ana":43},"#condition.damaged",{"layout":45},{"p":46,"rs":47,"damage":51},"The text fills the face available below the cornice (and seems likely to have continued below), with probably a consistent left margin, but a less regular right margin, and some cramping in order to fit words/phrases to the line (as e.g. in line 1).",{"_":48,"ana":49,"ref":50},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"ana":52},"#text_condition.deteriorated",{"lettering":54,"dimensions":161},[55,56],"The letters are mostly regular with a fairly square module and terminal points to the strokes rather than serifs. Alpha has broken cross-bar; epsilon has nearly equal bars; zeta in the form of an I with broad crossbars; kappa has short arms; mu has sloping outer strokes and half-height mid-strokes; omicron is nearly full-size, and consistently has a central dot (in lines 2 and 3 appears to have a line underneath); rho has rounded closed eye; sigma has horizontal top and bottom strokes, and the mid-strokes extend almost the full width; phi is standard height, elliptical; omega is consistently a closed circle (without the central dot of omicron), sometimes on the baseline, sometimes traversed by the line.",{"_":57,"ref":58},"\n                                    Types list:\n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n                                    \n      